               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>s. xiii in.--xv in.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_170">Darlington, Co.
                        Durham. Collegiate church of St Cuthbert. </orgName><p>The volume contains
                        the ex dono of Richard Witton, first dean of the college, and the list of
                        books dated 1487 'in isto librario' (SC222). 'Iste liber legatur ecclesie
                        colleg' de derlyngton per magistrum Ric' Witton' primum decanum ibidem Et
                        decanus habebit vsum [. .] tociens indeget reparacionem decanus reparabit
                        sumptibus suis propriis', at end, erased, but legible under u-v
                        light.</p><p>A volume made of three booklets but annotated by the same
                        15th-cent. hand, to show they were together by the time the book arrived at
                        Darlington.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Richard Witton (d. by 1451), first dean of
                     the college.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Capt. T. F. Powell, Sharow, Ripon. Thomas
                     Hopper, a former owner, was Capt. Powell's great great uncle: he 'was a Durham
                     man and lived in the Bailey near the Cathedral'.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Purchased by Mr Harold Smith of Leicester,
                     and given by him to Durham UL in 1988.</provenance>
               </history>
            </msDesc>
